# What Vercel does NOT need.
#
# This repo has two deployment targets (see CLAUDE.md): GitHub Pages serves the
# whole site at melbostads.com, and Vercel serves only `api/*.js`. Without this
# file Vercel uploads and stores the *entire* repository on every deployment —
# 171 MB, of which the API uses about 1.5 MB — and a free team gets 10 GB of
# deployment storage in total. At ~171 MB a deployment and a commit every four
# hours from the roster sync, that ceiling arrives in well under a hundred
# deployments. It did.
#
# `vercel.json`'s ignoreCommand does not help here: it skips the *build*, not
# the source upload, so a skipped deployment still costs the same storage as a
# real one.
#
# Nothing here affects GitHub Pages. Pages serves from the git repository and
# has never read this file, so every path excluded below is still live at
# melbostads.com — which is exactly why it is safe to drop them from Vercel.
#
# What the functions actually need, and why this list is a denylist rather than
# an allowlist: `api/**` (including `api/lib/`), `scripts/lib/providers.mjs`
# (imported by live-scoring.js and submit-lineup.js — it is self-contained and
# pulls in nothing else), `config/leagues.json` (read from disk at runtime by
# both of those), plus package.json and vercel.json. Everything below was
# checked against that list; nothing under `api/` references any of it.

# ---- The 166 MB that is pure static art ------------------------------------
# Banners, logos and plaques hotlinked by the MyFantasyLeague league pages, plus
# 57 Photoshop sources that are never served to anyone. Referenced by zero HTML
# files in this repo and by nothing under api/.
mfl/
images/
nfticons/
fflicons/
*.gif
*.psd
*.pxm

# ---- The synced snapshot ----------------------------------------------------
# data/rosters.json is fetched by myffl.html with a *relative* URL, and
# myffl.html is served by Pages — so that fetch resolves against Pages and never
# touches Vercel. It is also the file the sync rewrites every four hours, which
# made it the most frequently re-uploaded thing here after the art.
data/

# ---- Repo furniture, not runtime -------------------------------------------
# Only the top-level entry points, tests and probes — none of which Vercel ever
# runs. scripts/lib/ is deliberately NOT excluded, because providers.mjs lives
# there and two functions import it.
scripts/*.mjs
.github/
*.md

# Belt and braces on the line above. Under .gitignore semantics `*` does not
# cross a `/`, so `scripts/*.mjs` matches only the top level and providers.mjs
# is safe — verified with `git ls-files -i -c --exclude-from=.vercelignore`.
# Under looser globbing (where `*` does cross `/`) that same pattern would eat
# `scripts/lib/providers.mjs` and take live-scoring and submit-lineup down with
# it, with nothing in this repo to catch it. This negation costs one line and
# makes the file correct under either reading. Do not remove it.
!scripts/lib/

# The HTML is deliberately kept, even though Pages is what actually serves it.
# It is well under a megabyte against the 169 MB this file removes, and
# excluding every static file would leave the deployment with no output
# directory at all — a needless new failure mode for no measurable saving.

# ---- Editor and OS droppings ------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.db
